ens":0.0,"input_tokens":1889.857142857143,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":113.14285714285714,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":41753.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":1284.0,"requests":3}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["4 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the write lock alone protects the on-branch `git reset --hard <merged>` from a concurrent mover, or add a tip-unchanged/CAS check symmetric with the off-branch `update-ref <old-tip>` guard (and reconcile: if the lock suffices, note why CAS is still used off-branch).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e","T7","T9"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.615,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'git update-ref refs/heads/<ref> <merged> <old-tip> — a compare-and-swap, so a concurrent mover aborts the heal instead of clobbering'","'When ref IS the checked-out branch: git reset --hard <merged>' — no tip-unchanged / CAS check stated","The introduction of CAS off-branch signals the plan does not treat the write lock alone as sufficient against concurrent movers, yet applies no such guard on-branch"],"finding":"The on-branch heal path uses `git reset --hard <merged>` with no compare-and-swap, while the off-branch path uses `git update-ref refs/heads/<ref> <merged> <old-tip>` precisely to make a concurrent mover abort rather than clobber. The plan justifies the CAS by distrusting concurrency, but the on-branch reset has no equivalent tip-unchanged check, leaving an asymmetric concurrency guarantee that the write lock is either sufficient for (in which case CAS off-branch is redundant) or is not (in which case reset --hard can clobber a concurrent move).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f66c7c13fbbe98d55","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 2 (_heal_locked, s3_doctor.py:136-143)","norm_id":"nd87347b0f63ea345","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A second doctor run or external `git branch -f`/commit advances refs/heads/<ref> after this heal read old-tip but before the on-branch reset --hard, silently clobbering the concurrent update"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"For the on-branch case, first `git update-ref refs/heads/<ref> <merged> <old-tip>` (CAS) and then fast-forward the worktree/index (e.g. `git reset --hard <merged>` only after the CAS succeeds), so both paths share the same abort-on-concurrent-move guarantee.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State that the CAS ref-move (step 2) MUST complete successfully BEFORE _publish_and_prune bundles refs/heads/<ref>, that a CAS failure aborts the heal without publishing or deleting any bundle, and clarify the write-lock scope now spans fold through ref-move (and the bundle read).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.435,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Today the write lock is opened INSIDE _fold_heads (s3_doctor.py:239) and released on return; step 4 now bundles 'refs/heads/<ref>' (plan: 'Bundle refs/heads/<ref> explicitly ... off-branch, HEAD no longer names the merged tip')","Step 2 uses a compare-and-swap 'git update-ref refs/heads/<ref> <merged> <old-tip>' that by design 'aborts the heal instead of clobbering' on a concurrent mover","If _publish_and_prune bundles refs/heads/<ref> before the CAS moves it, the published bundle carries the stale tip; if the CAS aborts, the plan does not say publish/prune is skipped"],"finding":"The plan splits fold (step 1, holds the write lock internally), CAS ref-move (step 2), and bundle-publish+prune (step 4) across three functions without pinning the ordering between the ref-move and the publish, nor stating that a CAS failure aborts before publish/prune.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff6b837bc06584916","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan steps 2 and 4; s3_doctor.py:239-261 (lock scope), :264-317 (_publish_and_prune)","norm_id":"n43ca941b29e24df9","priority":0.165,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":["A concurrent writer moves refs/heads/<ref> between fold-start and the CAS: CAS aborts, but publish/prune may have already written the merged bundle and deleted originals","Off-branch heal where the ref-move and bundle-publish execute in the wrong order, bundling refs/heads/<ref> at its pre-move tip"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In _heal_locked, hold the write lock across fold, CAS ref-move, and publish/prune; sequence as fold -> CAS update-ref (or reset --hard on-branch) -> bundle refs/heads/<ref> -> prune, and treat a non-zero update-ref (stale <old-tip>) as an S3DoctorConflict-style abort that publishes and deletes nothing. Add a test asserting no bundle is written/deleted when the ref moves out from under the CAS.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.75,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The plan asserts merge=ours derived-file-collision coverage 'already exist[s] in test_s3_doctor_heldout.py:81' and must stay green, but line 81 is test_heal_unions_unrelated_history_head (an unrelated-history/orphan union test), and no merge=ours / .bridge_state derived-file collision test exists anywhere in that file (grep for 'merge=ours', 'ours', 'bridge_state' = no matches). The AC '.bridge_state/* merge=ours still resolves derived-file collisions in the fold' therefore has no guarding test, despite the plan switching the merge mechanism (git merge -> git merge-tree --write-tree) exactly where driver-honouring could regress.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe2eb9ca0ca5c0cbc","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 5 ('merge=ours and real-conflict coverage already exist in test_s3_doctor_heldout.py:81,109') and AC '.bridge_state/* merge=ours still resolves derived-file collisions in the fold'","norm_id":"nca51d67f15c1e1a6","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a heldout heal test that seeds two bundle heads which both write a conflicting .bridge_state/* file, run the merge-tree fold, and assert the fold resolves via merge=ours (keeps OUR copy) rather than raising S3DoctorConflict; stop citing :81 as merge=ours coverage.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"99777e42388758ad","material_parts":{"children":